      >
      <button
        type="button"
        aria-controls="capstoneCase"
        aria-selected="false"
        class="tab-button min-w-0"
        data-category="capstoneCase"
        id="tab-capstone-case"
        role="tab"
        ><h3>Case 2: Faculty evaluation workflow</h3></button
      >
    </div>

    <div
      id="redesignCase"
      class="case-category cs-wide"
      role="tabpanel"
      aria-labelledby="tab-redesign-case"
    >
      <div class="cs-hero-media cs-wide flex md:flex-row gap-4 overflow-x-auto lg:justify-center">
        <Image
          src={sageConfigurePage}
          alt="UT Sage product sample page"
          width={3000}
          quality={100}
          class="rounded-xl object-cover"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="cs-meta cs-wide">
        <MetaItem label="Project type">
          <p class="cs-inline-result">Professional experience, design system</p>
        </MetaItem>
        <MetaItem label="My role">
          <p class="cs-inline-result">Product Designer</p>
        </MetaItem>
        <MetaItem label="Tools">
          <Chip title="Figma" level="professional" showLevel={false}>
            <Icon slot="icon" name="figma-brands-solid-full" size={18} aria-hidden />
          </Chip>
          <Chip title="GitHub" level="professional" showLevel={false}>
            <Icon slot="icon" name="github" size={18} aria-hidden />
          </Chip>
        </MetaItem>
      </div>

      <StatRow>
        <Stat value="25+" label="components in the new design system" />
        <Stat value="9 mo" label="of reshaping the UX" />
        <Stat value="WCAG 2.2 AA" label="accessibility target" />
      </StatRow>

      <CaseStudyQuestion question="How do you turn a fragmented interface into one experience that scales?">
        <p class="project-description">
          When I joined as the sole designer, UT Sage had just launched its beta to
          faculty and students across UT Austin. The core features worked, but the
          interface felt fragmented, with inconsistent design, accessibility gaps,
          and missed UI details that left users confused and frustrated. My goal was
          a unified, accessible experience that could grow with the product, and
          look good too.
        </p>
      </CaseStudyQuestion>

      <SectionHeading index="01" title="Where do I start?" id="where-do-i-start" />
      <div class="cs-section-body">
        <p class="project-description">
          I started by testing the platform myself and found inconsistent icons,
          font sizes, and styles, plus major accessibility issues like poor
          contrast, small text, and no keyboard navigation. That is when I decided
          to rebuild the design system from scratch.
        </p>
        <div
          class="flex flex-row flex-wrap gap-4 min-w-0 w-full items-center"
        >
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-[min(280px,100%)] overflow-hidden">
            <Image
