        id="get-feedback-from-the-users-and-stakeholders"
      />
      <div class="cs-section-body">
        <p class="project-description">
          Before designing, I learned the existing design language. I asked the
          previous designer about her rationale, requested lo-fi sketches from my
          manager to see how the product evolved, and gathered regular feedback from
          my manager, who summarized insights from users and researchers.
        </p>
        <Image
          src={sageLofi}
          alt="UT Sage lo-fi design"
          width={2400}
          quality={100}
          class="rounded-xl object-cover"
        />
        <Image
          src={sageOriginalToggle}
          alt="UT Sage original toggle design"
          width={2400}
          quality={100}
          class="rounded-xl object-cover"
        />
      </div>

      <SectionHeading
        index="03"
        title="Build the new design system"
        id="build-the-new-design-system"
      />
      <div class="cs-section-body">
        <p class="project-description">
          I created a new design system of 25+ standardized components, built to
          meet WCAG 2.2 Level AA at the component level and backed by Figma tokens
          from the start, so it scales and stays future-proof.
        </p>
        <Image
          src={sageFoundations}
          alt="UT Sage foundations"
          width={1518}
          quality={100}
          class="rounded-xl object-cover"
        />
        <Image
          src={sageButtons}
          alt="UT Sage buttons"
          width={2400}
          quality={100}
          class="rounded-xl object-cover"
        />
        <Image
