            <strong>Toggle redesign</strong>
            <Image
              src={sageToggleIteration}
              alt="UT Sage toggle iteration"
              width={2400}
              quality={100}
              class="rounded-xl object-cover"
            />
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-center">
            <strong>Edit page</strong>
            <Image
              src={sageEditPage}
              alt="UT Sage edit page"
              width={2400}
              quality={100}
              class="rounded-xl object-cover"
            />
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-center">
            <strong>Home screen</strong>
            <Image
              src={sageHomepageTransition}
              alt="UT Sage homepage transition"
              width={2400}
              quality={100}
              class="rounded-xl object-cover"
            />
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-center">
            <strong>Help center</strong>
            <Image
              src={sageHelpCenterPage}
              alt="UT Sage help center page"
              width={2400}
              quality={100}
              class="rounded-xl object-cover"
            />
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-center">
            <strong>Example sharing flow, with redlines</strong>
            <Image
              src={sageSharingFlow}
              alt="UT Sage sharing flow"
              width={1722}
              quality={100}
              class="rounded-xl object-cover"
            />
            <p>Updated sharing flow with more accessible font sizes and colors.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <SectionHeading
        index="05"
        title="Validation & results"
        id="validation-and-results"
      />
      <div class="cs-section-body">
        <p class="project-description">
          After nine months, I delivered a more accessible, unified UT Sage
          prototype. The engineering team used my design system to rebuild
          pages quickly, with better consistency and accessibility.
        </p>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-8 items-center">
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-center">
            <strong>Home screen</strong>
            <Image
              src={sageHomepageProduction}
              alt="UT Sage homepage production"
              width={2400}
              quality={100}
              class="rounded-xl object-cover"
            />
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-center">
            <strong>Edit screen</strong>
            <Image
              src={sageEditPageProduction}
              alt="UT Sage edit page production"
              width={2400}
              quality={100}
              class="rounded-xl object-cover"
            />
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-center">
            <strong>Chat screen</strong>
            <Image
              src={sageChatPageProduction}
              alt="UT Sage chat page production"
              width={2400}
              quality={100}
              class="rounded-xl object-cover"
            />
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <SectionHeading index="06" title="Outcomes" id="outcomes" />
      <div class="cs-section-body">
        <p class="project-description">
          This redesign transformed UT Sage from a half-finished beta into a
          coherent, accessible educational platform.
        </p>
        <div class="cs-card-grid">
          <Card title="Accessibility" cardType="outline">
            <p>Aiming for WCAG 2.2 Level AA compliance across all components, addressing color contrast, font sizing, and keyboard navigation.</p>
          </Card>
          <Card title="Consistency" cardType="outline">
            <p>A 25+ component design system with Figma tokens keeps the design consistent across the platform.</p>
          </Card>
          <Card title="Developer efficiency" cardType="outline">
            <p>The engineering team can build pages significantly faster with the systematized design system.</p>
          </Card>
          <Card title="Design sustainability" cardType="outline">
            <p>When new features are added, their pages can be designed quickly on top of a robust design system.</p>
          </Card>
        </div>
      </div>

      <SectionHeading
        index="07"
        title="Reflection & next steps"
        id="reflection-and-next-steps"
      />
      <div class="cs-section-body">
        <p class="project-description">
          A solid design system is essential for scalable, high-quality results, and
          my design engineering skills helped bridge design and development. If I
          did it again, I would ask for more detailed feedback from users and
          stakeholders, which could have improved some design decisions and user
          flows.
        </p>
        <p class="cs-subhead">Next steps</p>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 project-description">
          <li>Implement dark mode to improve accessibility and user choice.</li>
          <li>Run broader user testing to gather feedback from diverse faculty and student populations.</li>
          <li>Make iterative improvements based on testing insights to keep refining the experience.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
